  <data name="PersonalSpaceName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0}'s Space</value>
    <comment>The name of the Space provisioned at registration. {0} is the Account's display name, so "Lee" gives "Lee's Space". Translators: the English possessive apostrophe is not universal - Finnish inflects the noun, Japanese uses a particle, and several languages have no possessive construction at all. Render the relationship the way the target language does rather than transliterating this one. Sentence case, never uppercase: any uppercasing is applied by CSS text-transform, because a resource holding an uppercased string is spelled out letter by letter by screen readers.</comment>
  </data>
